1
00:00:06,172 --> 00:00:07,507
She's better off this way.

2
00:00:09,217 --> 00:00:10,051
Yes.

3
00:00:13,888 --> 00:00:15,140
This is better for her.

4
00:00:16,224 --> 00:00:17,767
I'll only get her killed,

5
00:00:18,351 --> 00:00:19,643
just like my sister.

6
00:00:19,644 --> 00:00:23,565
<i>She's better off this way.
I'll get her killed. Better this way.</i>

7
00:00:27,068 --> 00:00:29,111
I'm sorry.

8
00:00:29,112 --> 00:00:30,572
Miss, are you okay?

9
00:00:33,575 --> 00:00:34,743
I've got you.

10
00:00:48,715 --> 00:00:50,925
Ms. Chang? Chang Ruyi, right?

11
00:00:52,260 --> 00:00:54,011
Come on, let's get you up.

12
00:00:54,012 --> 00:00:55,263
Up you go.

13
00:00:58,183 --> 00:00:59,683
Are you all right?

14
00:00:59,684 --> 00:01:00,977
Who are you?

15
00:01:01,686 --> 00:01:03,270
I'm a hospital volunteer.

16
00:01:03,271 --> 00:01:06,690
I saw you outside
the psychiatry department earlier.

17
00:01:06,691 --> 00:01:08,193
Do you need any help?

18
00:01:11,738 --> 00:01:15,283
Or are you going somewhere?
I can walk with you for a bit.

19
00:01:19,954 --> 00:01:24,709
I saw you holding a baby earlier.
Is your child in the hospital?

20
00:01:26,711 --> 00:01:28,504
None of your business.

21
00:01:28,505 --> 00:01:29,798
Leave me alone.

22
00:02:38,116 --> 00:02:39,325
It's so bright.

23
00:02:40,451 --> 00:02:42,327
Go make her some formula.

24
00:02:42,328 --> 00:02:43,454
Hurry, hurry.

25
00:02:44,998 --> 00:02:46,123
Just a second, okay?

26
00:02:46,124 --> 00:02:49,252
YOUXIN MEDICAL CENTER

27
00:02:57,927 --> 00:02:59,137
Here...

28
00:03:13,026 --> 00:03:14,860
<i>You're officially a Birth Assistant.</i>

29
00:03:14,861 --> 00:03:15,944
Welcome aboard!

30
00:03:15,945 --> 00:03:17,363
Congratulations!

31
00:03:18,656 --> 00:03:19,907
Thank you.

32
00:03:19,908 --> 00:03:21,408
That's great!

33
00:03:21,409 --> 00:03:22,993
Thank you so much.

34
00:03:22,994 --> 00:03:24,119
Congratulations!

35
00:03:24,120 --> 00:03:25,704
Thank you.

36
00:03:25,705 --> 00:03:26,663
Congratulations!

37
00:03:26,664 --> 00:03:28,123
Thank you.

38
00:03:28,124 --> 00:03:29,626
So?

39
00:03:33,129 --> 00:03:36,256
New moms have it hard. They're exhausted.

40
00:03:36,257 --> 00:03:38,675
Should we check on them and help out?

41
00:03:38,676 --> 00:03:40,177
Newborns are hard enough.

42
00:03:40,178 --> 00:03:41,970
Who has time for the moms?

43
00:03:41,971 --> 00:03:43,597
Moms have it tough too,

44
00:03:43,598 --> 00:03:47,018
but our goal is still
to help more babies be born safely.

45
00:04:13,461 --> 00:04:14,796
Why isn't she picking up?

46
00:04:16,547 --> 00:04:17,966
Is she still mad at me?

47
00:04:22,262 --> 00:04:23,804
Hello, Brother Xiao.

48
00:04:23,805 --> 00:04:24,973
I'm out now.

49
00:04:29,269 --> 00:04:31,938
What's been taken care of? Brother Xiao?

50
00:04:33,231 --> 00:04:35,400
What do you mean?

51
00:04:39,779 --> 00:04:41,197
You're back, A-Li!

52
00:04:45,285 --> 00:04:47,036
Do you smell something burning?

53
00:04:49,205 --> 00:04:50,873
What happened to the kitchen?

54
00:04:53,918 --> 00:04:57,130
It's a mess. Why is the formula left open?

55
00:04:58,923 --> 00:05:01,426
Didn't you promise to take care of her?

56
00:05:03,136 --> 00:05:05,595
- This...
- She's postpartum. Can she even drink?

57
00:05:05,596 --> 00:05:09,182
Not the point. Calm down.
We haven't seen Taozi all day.

58
00:05:09,183 --> 00:05:11,102
Why don't you ask where she is?

59
00:05:12,020 --> 00:05:13,895
You lost Taozi too?

60
00:05:13,896 --> 00:05:15,732
You two, seriously...

61
00:05:17,483 --> 00:05:18,568
Chang Ruyi.

62
00:05:19,777 --> 00:05:20,903
Chang Ruyi.

63
00:05:22,113 --> 00:05:24,157
Chang Ruyi, wake up. Where's Taozi?

64
00:05:25,491 --> 00:05:26,867
What are you doing here?

65
00:05:26,868 --> 00:05:28,745
You stink of alcohol.

66
00:05:29,787 --> 00:05:32,373
- Chang Ruyi, where's Taozi?
- I gave her away.

67
00:05:33,666 --> 00:05:35,000
Gave her away?

68
00:05:35,001 --> 00:05:37,378
Don't joke about that. Seriously, Ruyi?

69
00:05:38,671 --> 00:05:41,465
She probably just left Taozi with someone.

70
00:05:41,466 --> 00:05:43,800
Yeah. Maybe she's with the man downstairs?

71
00:05:43,801 --> 00:05:44,844
How could that be?

72
00:05:45,553 --> 00:05:48,889
Mom, diaper rash is very common in babies.

73
00:05:48,890 --> 00:05:51,434
Just apply the medicine as prescribed.

74
00:05:52,226 --> 00:05:55,896
I'm telling you, you need this too.
Premium baby oil.

75
00:05:55,897 --> 00:05:57,481
Here, put a little on.

76
00:05:57,482 --> 00:06:01,610
No. Baby oil will only make it worse.

77
00:06:01,611 --> 00:06:04,113
Over ten times a day is too much.

78
00:06:08,159 --> 00:06:09,618
Let the pros handle it.

79
00:06:09,619 --> 00:06:11,328
No, come here. Listen to me.

80
00:06:11,329 --> 00:06:14,707
Little Rice Cake can't sleep.
Is she feeling sick?

81
00:06:15,792 --> 00:06:16,917
No.

82
00:06:16,918 --> 00:06:19,336
You keep coming over
to hold and fuss over her.

83
00:06:19,337 --> 00:06:20,838
How can she sleep?

84
00:06:21,547 --> 00:06:23,382
You heard me talking that quietly?

85
00:06:30,640 --> 00:06:31,765
Sorry about earlier.

86
00:06:31,766 --> 00:06:33,308
- Don't mind it.
- No worries.

87
00:06:33,309 --> 00:06:34,935
I wanted to ask

88
00:06:34,936 --> 00:06:39,773
if the hospital's security cameras
caught who left the baby at my door.

89
00:06:39,774 --> 00:06:44,528
We checked,
but the cameras were down that day.

90
00:06:44,529 --> 00:06:46,113
That's great.

91
00:06:46,114 --> 00:06:48,782
Don't tell anyone about this, okay?

92
00:06:48,783 --> 00:06:50,201
"Anxiety disorder"?

93
00:06:52,286 --> 00:06:55,039
A ghost next door died
by suicide from postpartum depression.

94
00:06:56,082 --> 00:06:58,625
Postpartum depression. So she...

95
00:06:58,626 --> 00:07:00,545
She gave Taozi away.

96
00:07:04,340 --> 00:07:05,758
Be strong.

97
00:07:10,847 --> 00:07:11,973
Chang Ruyi?

98
00:07:13,933 --> 00:07:15,268
Chang Ruyi, you're awake.

99
00:07:16,018 --> 00:07:18,061
You left. Why come back?

100
00:07:18,062 --> 00:07:20,397
- Where's Taozi?
- I don't know.

101
00:07:20,398 --> 00:07:22,482
If she won't tell us, I'll possess her.

102
00:07:22,483 --> 00:07:24,902
Calm down. Let A-Li ask her.

103
00:07:25,945 --> 00:07:27,321
Where is Taozi now?

104
00:07:28,197 --> 00:07:29,698
That's none of your business.

105
00:07:29,699 --> 00:07:31,783
How is it none of my business?

106
00:07:31,784 --> 00:07:34,619
- Taozi, she...
- She was the first baby you cared for.

107
00:07:34,620 --> 00:07:36,830
- Taozi was my first baby.
- I even bathed her.

108
00:07:36,831 --> 00:07:37,747
I even bathed her.

109
00:07:37,748 --> 00:07:39,749
- And changed her diapers.
- I changed them too.

110
00:07:39,750 --> 00:07:41,668
- She smiles at me.
- Me too.

111
00:07:41,669 --> 00:07:43,211
Taozi really is adorable.

112
00:07:43,212 --> 00:07:44,463
So where is Taozi now?

113
00:07:44,464 --> 00:07:45,380
I gave her away.

114
00:07:45,381 --> 00:07:46,756
- I don't believe you.
- Enough.

115
00:07:46,757 --> 00:07:48,509
Calm down. Hold back.

116
00:07:49,510 --> 00:07:50,927
Don't believe me, then.

117
00:07:50,928 --> 00:07:52,889
She's your daughter.

118
00:07:58,102 --> 00:07:59,520
So, where is she?

119
00:08:05,193 --> 00:08:06,693
You don't need to know.

120
00:08:06,694 --> 00:08:07,987
Chang Ruyi!

121
00:08:08,571 --> 00:08:10,238
Let's go get her back.

122
00:08:10,239 --> 00:08:11,698
I'll help take care of her.

123
00:08:11,699 --> 00:08:14,744
You come and go as you please.
How can I trust you?

124
00:08:19,874 --> 00:08:21,541
You're just letting her go?

125
00:08:21,542 --> 00:08:22,792
You can't just do that.

126
00:08:22,793 --> 00:08:25,295
Pressuring her won't help.

127
00:08:25,296 --> 00:08:27,298
We have to wait until she gets better.

128
00:08:36,265 --> 00:08:37,600
Knock it off.

129
00:08:38,935 --> 00:08:40,685
Why is this happening?

130
00:08:40,686 --> 00:08:42,270
I said stop. What?

131
00:08:42,271 --> 00:08:43,730
My clothes reflect light.

132
00:08:43,731 --> 00:08:45,565
- It's not me, is it?
- What?

133
00:08:45,566 --> 00:08:46,858
Then why am I glowing?

134
00:08:46,859 --> 00:08:48,611
- Huh?
- So beautiful.

135
00:08:53,491 --> 00:08:55,825
Whose toy is hanging in the tree?

136
00:08:55,826 --> 00:08:58,329
No, that's a soul!

137
00:08:59,205 --> 00:09:00,331
Whose soul is that?

138
00:09:04,919 --> 00:09:06,336
Wait...

139
00:09:06,337 --> 00:09:07,922
Is that...

140
00:09:10,675 --> 00:09:12,342
That's the nerd?

141
00:09:12,343 --> 00:09:14,678
You said he disappeared, didn't you?

142
00:09:14,679 --> 00:09:18,224
I heard ghosts can look like this
before their souls disappear.

143
00:09:19,100 --> 00:09:22,143
The nerd can be annoying,
but this is really sad.

144
00:09:22,144 --> 00:09:23,603
Yeah. How tragic.

145
00:09:23,604 --> 00:09:25,230
Maybe he loved the wrong person.

146
00:09:25,231 --> 00:09:28,149
A-Li, burn incense twice a day. Save him.

147
00:09:28,150 --> 00:09:31,361
But what if he possesses me again?

148
00:09:31,362 --> 00:09:34,823
Didn't your grandma always say
to be generous and help others?

149
00:09:34,824 --> 00:09:36,116
People, not ghosts.

150
00:09:36,117 --> 00:09:37,576
She helped ghosts too.

151
00:09:37,577 --> 00:09:38,785
She helped us all the time.

152
00:09:38,786 --> 00:09:40,912
She'd burn offerings for us
and pray to us.

153
00:09:40,913 --> 00:09:45,209
A-Li, do good while you're alive,
or you'll die with regrets.

154
00:09:49,338 --> 00:09:52,758
Why be so nice to her?
You're even cooking for her.

155
00:09:53,718 --> 00:09:55,844
She looks really worn out.

156
00:09:55,845 --> 00:09:58,264
She probably hasn't eaten properly
in a while.

157
00:09:59,056 --> 00:10:03,019
I'm impressed.
You can really let bygones be bygones.

158
00:10:04,937 --> 00:10:06,813
Now that we know Ruyi is ill,

159
00:10:06,814 --> 00:10:08,857
we should be more understanding.

160
00:10:08,858 --> 00:10:11,110
Don't let her emotions affect you.

161
00:10:11,777 --> 00:10:14,821
Are you talking to yourself?
She can't even see us.

162
00:10:14,822 --> 00:10:16,906
This kid really cares about her.

163
00:10:16,907 --> 00:10:18,117
You like Chang Ruyi?

164
00:10:19,535 --> 00:10:21,453
No, I don't.

165
00:10:21,454 --> 00:10:23,330
- I...
- He likes Chang Ruyi.

166
00:10:23,331 --> 00:10:24,999
No, I just...

167
00:10:25,833 --> 00:10:28,335
I... I just like cooking, that's all.

168
00:10:28,336 --> 00:10:29,586
You do like her.

169
00:10:29,587 --> 00:10:31,838
No, I just like cooking.

170
00:10:31,839 --> 00:10:33,673
Scrambling eggs and stuff.

171
00:10:33,674 --> 00:10:34,799
Is it really love?

172
00:10:34,800 --> 00:10:39,013
No, I just like making simple dishes,
that's all.

173
00:10:50,149 --> 00:10:51,775
You're up.

174
00:10:51,776 --> 00:10:52,942
Have some breakfast.

175
00:10:52,943 --> 00:10:56,072
Remember to take your medicine.
I'll go to your follow-up with you.

176
00:10:56,697 --> 00:10:58,199
Stay out of my business.

177
00:11:00,201 --> 00:11:02,662
You're going out? Where are you going?

178
00:11:03,537 --> 00:11:04,705
Chang Ruyi?

179
00:11:28,396 --> 00:11:29,605
She didn't eat it?

180
00:11:30,898 --> 00:11:32,899
Damn, I thought she would.

181
00:11:32,900 --> 00:11:34,944
Women really do know women best.

182
00:11:35,903 --> 00:11:37,988
- All of them.
- Save two for me.

183
00:11:41,909 --> 00:11:44,370
Go after her! She's already downstairs.

184
00:11:45,955 --> 00:11:47,038
Should I go?

185
00:11:47,039 --> 00:11:48,165
Go.

186
00:11:49,125 --> 00:11:50,083
CHANG RUYI

187
00:11:50,084 --> 00:11:53,921
Your last livestreaming job
was months ago.

188
00:11:54,713 --> 00:11:55,923
Why did you quit?

189
00:11:57,007 --> 00:11:58,467
Family reasons.

190
00:12:01,053 --> 00:12:03,388
You ran group buys from home too.

191
00:12:03,389 --> 00:12:04,765
How did it go?

192
00:12:05,766 --> 00:12:07,809
<i>- She sold fakes.
- They gave me an allergic reaction.</i>

193
00:12:07,810 --> 00:12:09,644
<i>- Rash all over. Almost died!
- Call the cops.</i>

194
00:12:09,645 --> 00:12:11,522
- Ms. Chang.
<i>- Pay up or we call cops.</i>

195
00:12:12,982 --> 00:12:14,692
I'll work hard.

196
00:12:15,401 --> 00:12:17,652
My livestream sales
were really good before.

197
00:12:17,653 --> 00:12:20,656
I've seen your livestreams.
I have confidence in you.

198
00:12:21,323 --> 00:12:24,118
But I need to ask something.

199
00:12:25,035 --> 00:12:27,705
Are you planning to get married
or have kids soon?

200
00:12:30,458 --> 00:12:32,084
I'm not getting married...

201
00:12:33,252 --> 00:12:34,879
or pregnant anytime soon.

202
00:12:36,839 --> 00:12:39,758
Pregnancy and motherhood
are really hard, you know?

203
00:12:40,426 --> 00:12:43,011
No need to explain.
Our policy on pregnancy--

204
00:12:43,012 --> 00:12:45,054
Society is really unfair to mothers.

205
00:12:45,055 --> 00:12:48,725
Do you know how hard it is to work
and raise a child while pregnant?

206
00:12:48,726 --> 00:12:50,727
They endure it all
to give them a better life.

207
00:12:50,728 --> 00:12:54,190
No matter how hard it gets,
they keep going...

208
00:13:04,909 --> 00:13:06,702
I don't have a child.

209
00:13:10,831 --> 00:13:12,124
I'll work hard.

210
00:13:14,168 --> 00:13:15,377
Please give me a chance.

211
00:13:30,559 --> 00:13:31,434
I'm sorry.

212
00:13:31,435 --> 00:13:33,229
- Are you okay?
- I'm fine.

213
00:13:35,981 --> 00:13:37,024
What's wrong?

214
00:13:38,234 --> 00:13:40,444
You... You don't remember me?

215
00:13:43,405 --> 00:13:45,698
I'm the hospital volunteer
from the other day.

216
00:13:45,699 --> 00:13:47,034
I helped you pick up...

217
00:13:49,578 --> 00:13:51,788
I'm sorry. I was in a bad place that day.

218
00:13:51,789 --> 00:13:53,164
That's why I was so rude.

219
00:13:53,165 --> 00:13:56,502
It's okay. I know you just had a baby.

220
00:13:58,128 --> 00:14:00,296
There's a lot of pressure.

221
00:14:00,297 --> 00:14:02,215
You want to care for your baby,

222
00:14:02,216 --> 00:14:03,508
but nothing seems to go right.

223
00:14:03,509 --> 00:14:08,597
Then you start feeling like a failure,
and the pressure builds. Right?

224
00:14:11,684 --> 00:14:13,519
Feeling better now?

225
00:14:16,855 --> 00:14:18,232
Want to talk?

226
00:14:22,152 --> 00:14:23,571
I'll stay with you.

227
00:14:28,909 --> 00:14:31,077
Here, have an apple.

228
00:14:31,078 --> 00:14:32,871
The peel is really nutritious.

229
00:14:32,872 --> 00:14:34,455
- Here.
- I can't eat, thanks.

230
00:14:34,456 --> 00:14:36,041
Take it home for later.

231
00:14:40,838 --> 00:14:44,049
Even if you have no appetite,
you need to eat.

232
00:14:45,342 --> 00:14:48,679
You barely eat, and you're way too thin.

233
00:14:54,393 --> 00:14:55,853
Being a mom is hard.

234
00:14:59,982 --> 00:15:02,109
Why is your child hospitalized?

235
00:15:04,528 --> 00:15:09,616
If you're too busy,
I can check on her while I volunteer.

236
00:15:09,617 --> 00:15:10,951
What room is she in?

237
00:15:13,162 --> 00:15:14,454
No, it's okay.

238
00:15:14,455 --> 00:15:15,830
I have to go.

239
00:15:15,831 --> 00:15:16,999
Thanks for the apple.

240
00:15:23,505 --> 00:15:25,173
Sure, it's just...

241
00:15:25,174 --> 00:15:27,175
My husband and I split the work.

242
00:15:27,176 --> 00:15:30,596
He handles baths,
and I play with the baby.

243
00:15:31,639 --> 00:15:33,014
My next baby's a boy.

244
00:15:33,015 --> 00:15:35,475
- Having two kids really is...
- Taozi.

245
00:15:35,476 --> 00:15:36,684
What are you doing?

246
00:15:36,685 --> 00:15:38,895
Sorry.

247
00:15:38,896 --> 00:15:41,064
My friend just loves kids.

248
00:15:41,065 --> 00:15:42,858
Your child's so cute, that's why.

249
00:15:45,778 --> 00:15:46,819
I didn't mean to.

250
00:15:46,820 --> 00:15:48,489
I don't know why that happened.

251
00:15:57,206 --> 00:15:58,874
Where did Ruyi go?

252
00:16:04,171 --> 00:16:06,715
I live here. Thank you.

253
00:16:07,341 --> 00:16:10,052
Anyone at home to care for you?

254
00:16:10,928 --> 00:16:12,721
I'm fine. Thanks.

255
00:16:13,555 --> 00:16:16,307
You're still young.
Remember to take your medication.

256
00:16:16,308 --> 00:16:20,562
I had a friend with postpartum depression
who didn't take hers,

257
00:16:21,563 --> 00:16:24,108
and she did something
she'll regret for the rest of her life.

258
00:16:24,733 --> 00:16:26,735
She still regrets it to this day.

259
00:16:29,947 --> 00:16:32,324
I'll take my meds. Thanks.

260
00:16:50,134 --> 00:16:51,259
Chang Ruyi!

261
00:16:51,260 --> 00:16:53,470
I left breakfast outside your door.

262
00:16:54,888 --> 00:16:56,348
Remember to eat.

263
00:17:01,478 --> 00:17:03,522
Chang Ruyi, lunch is ready.

264
00:17:06,942 --> 00:17:09,987
I made hot soup.
Come have some while it's warm.

265
00:17:17,536 --> 00:17:19,120
What's gotten into her?

266
00:17:19,121 --> 00:17:22,123
She won't eat or take her meds,
and she's drinking too!

267
00:17:22,124 --> 00:17:23,708
What is she doing to herself?

268
00:17:23,709 --> 00:17:25,168
Calm down.

269
00:17:25,169 --> 00:17:29,088
- We need to be more patient with her.
- How can I be patient?

270
00:17:29,089 --> 00:17:30,757
Isn't she still breastfeeding?

271
00:17:30,758 --> 00:17:33,719
If Taozi gets a sip, won't she be woozy?

272
00:17:36,221 --> 00:17:38,891
Uncle, this is no time for jokes.

273
00:17:39,808 --> 00:17:41,351
Say something helpful.

274
00:17:42,019 --> 00:17:43,478
All right, I'm sorry.

275
00:17:43,479 --> 00:17:45,063
What do we do?

276
00:17:45,064 --> 00:17:46,981
- Make her take meds?
- She won't.

277
00:17:46,982 --> 00:17:49,777
Then think of something.
Pry her mouth open, or...

278
00:17:50,694 --> 00:17:52,904
Take her outside for a walk, get some sun.

279
00:17:52,905 --> 00:17:54,781
Only she can help herself.

280
00:17:54,782 --> 00:17:56,699
So, is this just some kind of avoidance?

281
00:17:56,700 --> 00:17:58,409
- Shush!
- Not funny?

282
00:17:58,410 --> 00:18:00,161
Sorry.

283
00:18:00,162 --> 00:18:01,789
Did you hear it?

284
00:18:04,583 --> 00:18:05,876
I'll check on her.

285
00:18:11,256 --> 00:18:13,550
She's crying holding Taozi's pacifier.

286
00:18:17,763 --> 00:18:19,056
Chang Ruyi.

287
00:18:28,107 --> 00:18:31,484
Chang Ruyi,
I made some of your favorite food.

288
00:18:31,485 --> 00:18:34,696
It's still hot,
so come eat while it's warm.

289
00:18:35,989 --> 00:18:37,241
Chang Ruyi...

290
00:18:38,659 --> 00:18:40,034
Chang Ruyi?

291
00:18:40,035 --> 00:18:41,495
Sit down. I'll get you a bowl.

292
00:18:42,079 --> 00:18:45,706
Ruyi, don't do this to yourself.
Just eat something first.

293
00:18:45,707 --> 00:18:46,624
Here...

294
00:18:46,625 --> 00:18:49,043
Chang Ruyi, you can't drink beer.

295
00:18:49,044 --> 00:18:51,045
You can't drink beer.
You're still recovering.

296
00:18:51,046 --> 00:18:54,883
How about some rice first?
You haven't eaten anything, Ruyi.

297
00:18:56,677 --> 00:18:57,803
You...

298
00:19:19,449 --> 00:19:21,410
<i>Ruyi's getting worse.</i>

299
00:19:26,582 --> 00:19:29,877
And A-Li seems to be getting worse too.

300
00:19:31,336 --> 00:19:32,337
A-Li?

301
00:19:38,135 --> 00:19:42,431
Even though Ruyi closed the door,
you can be the one to open it.

302
00:19:52,524 --> 00:19:53,650
A-Li?

303
00:20:13,962 --> 00:20:16,756
<i>Just one bottle. Remember your meds.</i>

304
00:20:16,757 --> 00:20:18,717
<i>Wait 30... an hour.</i>

305
00:20:26,225 --> 00:20:27,767
<i>This is a famous turnip cake.</i>

306
00:20:27,768 --> 00:20:29,518
<i>It was my grandma's favorite.</i>

307
00:20:29,519 --> 00:20:31,230
<i>Hope you like it too.</i>

308
00:21:23,073 --> 00:21:24,199
Good morning.

309
00:21:30,289 --> 00:21:32,498
<i>Morning, Chang Ruyi.</i>

310
00:21:32,499 --> 00:21:35,835
<i>A beautiful day
starts with a good breakfast.</i>

311
00:21:35,836 --> 00:21:38,630
<i>Finish breakfast and take your meds.</i>

312
00:21:45,262 --> 00:21:47,431
<i>Door's locked.</i>

313
00:21:52,185 --> 00:21:58,442
<i>Eat breakfast, take your meds
and I'll open it.</i>

314
00:22:11,330 --> 00:22:12,581
<i>Is it good?</i>

315
00:22:14,416 --> 00:22:15,458
It's okay.

316
00:22:15,459 --> 00:22:18,378
Chang Ruyi...

317
00:22:21,089 --> 00:22:22,299
Chang Ruyi.

318
00:22:23,008 --> 00:22:24,508
Are you okay?

319
00:22:24,509 --> 00:22:26,093
So, what do you think?

320
00:22:26,094 --> 00:22:27,344
Does it look good?

321
00:22:27,345 --> 00:22:28,721
Why are you dressed like that?

322
00:22:28,722 --> 00:22:30,514
I saw these clothes piled up there,

323
00:22:30,515 --> 00:22:34,102
I figured you didn't want them,
so I'll take them.

324
00:22:37,481 --> 00:22:39,148
And this too.

325
00:22:39,149 --> 00:22:42,109
Taozi won't need
these bottles anymore, right?

326
00:22:42,110 --> 00:22:44,613
- I'll recycle it, then.
- Why wouldn't she need it?

327
00:22:45,197 --> 00:22:46,447
Then come get it.

328
00:22:46,448 --> 00:22:47,991
You're so annoying.

329
00:22:48,909 --> 00:22:50,660
Fine. You want it? Come get it.

330
00:22:54,623 --> 00:22:56,832
- Come on!
- Tseng Yu-Li!

331
00:22:56,833 --> 00:22:58,542
You're so childish. Give me the bottles!

332
00:22:58,543 --> 00:23:00,795
Come on! You don't want these.

333
00:23:00,796 --> 00:23:02,546
Hurry up!

334
00:23:02,547 --> 00:23:05,841
- Give it back!
- Wow, skirts are breezy!

335
00:23:05,842 --> 00:23:07,635
So breezy!

336
00:23:07,636 --> 00:23:10,054
Come on, hurry up!

337
00:23:10,055 --> 00:23:11,223
Tseng Yu-Li!

338
00:23:12,140 --> 00:23:13,849
- You're so annoying.
- Hurry up!

339
00:23:13,850 --> 00:23:15,518
You're almost there. Come on.

340
00:23:15,519 --> 00:23:16,936
Hurry!

341
00:23:16,937 --> 00:23:18,479
Chang Ruyi, come on!

342
00:23:18,480 --> 00:23:20,065
Hurry! Chang Ruyi.

343
00:23:22,192 --> 00:23:24,027
Climb up, Chang Ruyi.

344
00:23:26,071 --> 00:23:27,531
I think I'm too high up.

345
00:23:30,283 --> 00:23:31,742
Want some dried fruit?

346
00:23:31,743 --> 00:23:33,245
It'll cheer you up.

347
00:23:35,122 --> 00:23:36,247
So?

348
00:23:36,248 --> 00:23:37,999
Feel better after breaking a sweat?

349
00:23:41,670 --> 00:23:42,712
Much better.

350
00:23:43,505 --> 00:23:46,758
I'll take my meds and exercise more
so I can get better.

351
00:23:49,511 --> 00:23:51,929
It must be hard for you
with Taozi not around, right?

352
00:23:51,930 --> 00:23:55,015
But I didn't take good care of her
when she was with me.

353
00:23:55,016 --> 00:23:57,351
I put her in danger.

354
00:23:57,352 --> 00:23:59,645
I've seen how much you love Taozi.

355
00:23:59,646 --> 00:24:03,608
No one loves her more than you do.

356
00:24:04,359 --> 00:24:05,485
Really?

357
00:24:09,239 --> 00:24:11,407
So who did you give Taozi to?

358
00:24:11,408 --> 00:24:13,242
Let's go bring her home.

359
00:24:13,243 --> 00:24:14,786
I don't know them.

360
00:24:17,205 --> 00:24:18,373
Chang Ruyi,

361
00:24:18,999 --> 00:24:20,374
you mean to say

362
00:24:20,375 --> 00:24:23,461
you gave Taozi to someone
you don't even know?

363
00:24:50,530 --> 00:24:54,241
When can we take Little Rice Cake home?
I don't want to stay here.

364
00:24:54,242 --> 00:24:59,371
You suddenly wanted to redo the nursery.
Give the designer some time, okay?

365
00:24:59,372 --> 00:25:01,916
Tell him to hurry.

366
00:25:01,917 --> 00:25:04,585
Doesn't this cutie look like me?

367
00:25:04,586 --> 00:25:06,713
Of course. She's beautiful, just like you.

368
00:25:07,422 --> 00:25:08,256
Let's go.

369
00:25:17,724 --> 00:25:19,516
<i>I don't know who the other person is,</i>

370
00:25:19,517 --> 00:25:20,893
but who cares?

371
00:25:20,894 --> 00:25:22,937
I'm the baby's mother.

372
00:25:22,938 --> 00:25:25,857
I'll make sure my child
has all the love in the world.

373
00:25:27,484 --> 00:25:28,902
How could it be her?

374
00:25:33,657 --> 00:25:35,659
She'll probably take good care of Taozi.

375
00:25:36,409 --> 00:25:39,245
She loves children so much. It'll be okay.

376
00:25:39,246 --> 00:25:40,162
Okay, thank you.

377
00:25:40,163 --> 00:25:41,455
This is for the best.

378
00:25:41,456 --> 00:25:42,707
Ms. Chang.

379
00:25:44,209 --> 00:25:46,835
- Ma'am.
- What a coincidence seeing you here.

380
00:25:46,836 --> 00:25:49,964
Here for a follow-up or to see your child?

381
00:25:49,965 --> 00:25:51,508
How is she?

382
00:26:01,142 --> 00:26:02,769
It's okay.

383
00:26:04,396 --> 00:26:07,399
You know I gave my baby away.

384
00:26:08,692 --> 00:26:11,403
Don't you think I'm a terrible mother?

385
00:26:15,198 --> 00:26:17,200
I don't know what happened,

386
00:26:18,285 --> 00:26:22,706
but I know no mother
wants to abandon her child.

387
00:26:26,876 --> 00:26:31,506
You're sick right now,
so focus on getting better.

388
00:26:33,008 --> 00:26:35,927
You need to be healthy
to bring your child home, right?

389
00:26:40,098 --> 00:26:42,434
I didn't want to give her up.

390
00:26:46,146 --> 00:26:48,148
I should've seen a doctor sooner.

391
00:26:49,399 --> 00:26:52,652
If you're willing,
you can still bring your child home.

392
00:26:54,571 --> 00:26:55,697
You think so?

393
00:26:58,283 --> 00:26:59,784
You haven't had lunch, right?

394
00:27:00,368 --> 00:27:03,579
I'll get you something. Wait here.

395
00:27:03,580 --> 00:27:06,124
- No, it's okay.
- Sit here and rest for a bit.

396
00:27:21,723 --> 00:27:23,183
How did this happen?

397
00:28:43,138 --> 00:28:44,305
You're awake.

398
00:28:47,726 --> 00:28:52,479
I didn't know what you liked,
so I brought you a sandwich and some milk.

399
00:28:52,480 --> 00:28:53,773
Here, eat up.

400
00:28:55,483 --> 00:28:57,068
<i>Take good care of your little sister.</i>

401
00:29:02,824 --> 00:29:03,783
Mom.

402
00:29:25,305 --> 00:29:26,264
What do you want?

403
00:29:28,516 --> 00:29:32,311
You left us over 20 years ago.
Why come back now?

404
00:29:32,312 --> 00:29:34,022
I didn't abandon you.

405
00:29:40,361 --> 00:29:42,362
I left because of your father.

406
00:29:42,363 --> 00:29:44,615
He beat me every day.

407
00:29:44,616 --> 00:29:47,701
He abused me.
I had no choice but to divorce him.

408
00:29:47,702 --> 00:29:50,162
Don't come near me. Go away.

409
00:29:50,163 --> 00:29:51,456
No, please!

410
00:30:05,428 --> 00:30:07,388
Chang Ruyi, time to eat.

411
00:30:18,107 --> 00:30:19,442
She should be okay, right?

412
00:30:32,705 --> 00:30:34,414
Hey...

413
00:30:34,415 --> 00:30:36,376
It's on fire! You guys...

414
00:30:49,430 --> 00:30:50,889
Seriously?

415
00:30:50,890 --> 00:30:53,767
I have to take care of Ruyi
and all three of you too?

416
00:30:53,768 --> 00:30:58,773
- It's a rare opportunity.
- Maybe we'll reincarnate sooner.

417
00:30:59,357 --> 00:31:01,024
Look at yourselves.

418
00:31:01,025 --> 00:31:03,527
If you stopped scaring kids,
you'd have reincarnated by now.

419
00:31:03,528 --> 00:31:06,239
This isn't for the nerd. It's for you.

420
00:31:07,198 --> 00:31:08,240
Tadpoles!

421
00:31:08,241 --> 00:31:09,324
So cute!

422
00:31:09,325 --> 00:31:10,534
Is this normal?

423
00:31:10,535 --> 00:31:11,952
It keeps getting bigger.

424
00:31:11,953 --> 00:31:13,830
It's growing.

425
00:31:18,126 --> 00:31:19,502
The nerd is appearing!

426
00:31:21,546 --> 00:31:23,213
Can you hear us?

427
00:31:23,214 --> 00:31:25,007
You should thank us.

428
00:31:25,008 --> 00:31:27,343
Without us, A-Li wouldn't have saved you.

429
00:31:31,180 --> 00:31:32,390
Mr. Tseng,

430
00:31:33,016 --> 00:31:35,977
sorry I possessed you.

431
00:31:36,728 --> 00:31:37,978
Forget it.

432
00:31:37,979 --> 00:31:41,065
If I hadn't forgiven you,
I wouldn't have brought you back.

433
00:31:42,191 --> 00:31:44,193
I should thank you.

434
00:31:44,861 --> 00:31:47,696
At least I got to have dinner with Ruyi.

435
00:31:47,697 --> 00:31:49,406
You still haven't given up?

436
00:31:49,407 --> 00:31:51,408
I'm warning you, leave her alone.

437
00:31:51,409 --> 00:31:54,077
- Ruyi's been really--
- I know.

438
00:31:54,078 --> 00:31:55,830
I know all that.

439
00:31:56,873 --> 00:31:58,666
Thank you for always helping Ruyi.

440
00:32:05,006 --> 00:32:06,299
Mr. Tseng?

441
00:32:08,259 --> 00:32:13,181
I have a question for you,
but you have to answer honestly.

442
00:32:13,848 --> 00:32:15,058
What do you want to ask?

443
00:32:16,851 --> 00:32:18,394
Do you really love Ruyi?

444
00:32:19,479 --> 00:32:22,148
A hundred percent.
I'm serious about her. A-Li, tell him.

445
00:32:22,815 --> 00:32:27,027
What kind of question is that?
Do I have to answer now?

446
00:32:27,028 --> 00:32:28,820
Or wait until your next life?

447
00:32:28,821 --> 00:32:30,239
Say it now.

448
00:32:38,081 --> 00:32:39,082
Yeah.

449
00:32:42,752 --> 00:32:45,087
To me...

450
00:32:45,088 --> 00:32:47,464
Ruyi is just mean,
she's got a terrible temper,

451
00:32:47,465 --> 00:32:49,801
she's not gentle at all.

452
00:32:50,551 --> 00:32:51,761
And...

453
00:32:52,637 --> 00:32:54,305
Why are you sighing?

454
00:32:55,056 --> 00:32:59,142
But luckily, Taozi's adorable.
Otherwise, I would've lost it ages ago.

455
00:32:59,143 --> 00:33:02,605
You're basically saying Ruyi's cute.

456
00:33:03,481 --> 00:33:04,565
I mean...

457
00:33:06,317 --> 00:33:10,320
Chang Ruyi always looks so grumpy,

458
00:33:10,321 --> 00:33:13,032
but when she smiles,
she's pretty cute, right?

459
00:33:13,992 --> 00:33:16,159
Yeah.

460
00:33:16,160 --> 00:33:20,206
Well, after spending
these past few weeks together,

461
00:33:20,873 --> 00:33:24,377
it may seem like
I've been taking care of them, but...

462
00:33:26,337 --> 00:33:28,423
I actually like feeling

463
00:33:29,215 --> 00:33:30,925
needed and

464
00:33:32,135 --> 00:33:33,970
having someone around.

465
00:33:35,596 --> 00:33:37,890
I don't have any family anymore.

466
00:33:39,851 --> 00:33:41,435
And...

467
00:33:41,436 --> 00:33:43,563
It's the simple things, I guess.

468
00:33:44,355 --> 00:33:47,649
Having someone to talk to,

469
00:33:47,650 --> 00:33:49,901
eat with

470
00:33:49,902 --> 00:33:52,030
and raise a child with.

471
00:33:53,156 --> 00:33:57,201
Though raising a kid isn't simple at all.
It's hard.

472
00:33:58,536 --> 00:34:01,873
Maybe that's why...

473
00:34:02,749 --> 00:34:05,585
my life feels

474
00:34:08,004 --> 00:34:09,297
meaningful now.

475
00:34:11,924 --> 00:34:13,925
I didn't realize it

476
00:34:13,926 --> 00:34:16,344
until you possessed me
and had dinner with her.

477
00:34:16,345 --> 00:34:20,265
I felt weird afterward, right?
Really weird.

478
00:34:20,266 --> 00:34:22,351
My chest felt tight.

479
00:34:23,269 --> 00:34:24,728
Like...

480
00:34:24,729 --> 00:34:26,271
Clogged milk duct too?

481
00:34:26,272 --> 00:34:27,606
Your prostate is!

482
00:34:27,607 --> 00:34:29,107
That's jealousy.

483
00:34:29,108 --> 00:34:33,653
It wasn't really jealousy. It was...

484
00:34:33,654 --> 00:34:35,406
You like Ruyi?

485
00:34:47,043 --> 00:34:48,044
Yes.

486
00:34:48,795 --> 00:34:50,088
I like Chang Ruyi.

487
00:34:57,011 --> 00:35:00,181
Then I'll leave Ruyi in your care.

488
00:35:05,019 --> 00:35:06,395
And...

489
00:35:07,313 --> 00:35:09,982
Could you give her a message for me?

490
00:35:10,817 --> 00:35:12,734
Sure. What should I say?

491
00:35:12,735 --> 00:35:14,694
Or use my body

492
00:35:14,695 --> 00:35:16,364
and you can...

493
00:35:17,490 --> 00:35:19,324
- Give him some.
- Just a little.

494
00:35:19,325 --> 00:35:21,076
- Is that enough?
- Give him a sip.

495
00:35:21,077 --> 00:35:21,993
Just a little.

496
00:35:21,994 --> 00:35:23,246
Come here...

497
00:35:26,249 --> 00:35:28,792
The nerd did take care of you.

498
00:35:28,793 --> 00:35:32,713
He has something he wants to tell you.

499
00:35:35,591 --> 00:35:36,716
Right here?

500
00:35:36,717 --> 00:35:38,177
Yes. He's here.

501
00:35:38,845 --> 00:35:40,138
Say it.

502
00:35:41,764 --> 00:35:43,766
Come on, say it. I'll tell her for you.

503
00:35:48,396 --> 00:35:49,689
Hurry up.

504
00:35:50,565 --> 00:35:53,942
Chang Ruyi, I want to apologize to you.

505
00:35:53,943 --> 00:35:56,111
- Your acting is terrible.
- Just stop acting.

506
00:35:56,112 --> 00:35:57,904
- Damn.
- Nothing like him.

507
00:35:57,905 --> 00:36:00,907
Wait, are you pretending to be him?

508
00:36:00,908 --> 00:36:01,826
Yeah.

509
00:36:02,660 --> 00:36:03,869
Think this is funny?

510
00:36:03,870 --> 00:36:05,079
Sorry.

511
00:36:05,955 --> 00:36:07,582
He's not saying anything.

512
00:36:08,332 --> 00:36:10,750
- Can he hear me?
- Yeah.

513
00:36:10,751 --> 00:36:12,295
He's here, right?

514
00:36:13,462 --> 00:36:15,130
Listen, you idiot.

515
00:36:15,131 --> 00:36:17,592
What kind of ghost are you?
Stay away from me.

516
00:36:20,887 --> 00:36:23,096
Taozi and I are fine now.

517
00:36:23,097 --> 00:36:24,640
We don't need you anymore.

518
00:36:26,350 --> 00:36:27,685
Go reincarnate.

519
00:36:28,603 --> 00:36:29,937
Thank you...

520
00:36:31,314 --> 00:36:32,690
for taking care of us.

521
00:36:33,608 --> 00:36:35,067
Whenever we needed you,

522
00:36:36,194 --> 00:36:37,778
you were always there.

523
00:36:39,197 --> 00:36:40,907
I'm sorry this happened to you.

524
00:36:42,366 --> 00:36:43,701
I'm really sorry.

525
00:36:46,746 --> 00:36:49,206
I hope you have a good next life

526
00:36:49,207 --> 00:36:52,126
and find someone to truly love.

527
00:36:53,336 --> 00:36:54,670
Go reincarnate. We...

528
00:36:55,213 --> 00:36:56,714
We don't need you anymore.

529
00:36:57,340 --> 00:36:59,675
I'll burn as much incense as you want.

530
00:37:01,260 --> 00:37:02,261
Thank you.

531
00:37:05,514 --> 00:37:07,474
That was so touching, Ruyi.

532
00:37:07,475 --> 00:37:10,602
Is this modern female empowerment?

533
00:37:10,603 --> 00:37:12,855
- Was that okay? Did he hear me?
- Yeah.

534
00:37:14,440 --> 00:37:15,733
He looks really moved.

535
00:37:19,946 --> 00:37:21,446
What's wrong?

536
00:37:21,447 --> 00:37:23,491
He... He fainted.

537
00:37:24,325 --> 00:37:25,576
Is he okay?

538
00:37:26,285 --> 00:37:27,953
- Let him rest.
- I'll get the door.

539
00:37:27,954 --> 00:37:28,871
Coming!

540
00:37:31,916 --> 00:37:33,125
Who are you here for?

541
00:37:34,043 --> 00:37:35,627
You look really familiar.

542
00:37:35,628 --> 00:37:36,878
Who are you here for?

543
00:37:36,879 --> 00:37:38,630
I'm looking for A-Li. Is he here?

544
00:37:38,631 --> 00:37:40,590
A-Li, someone's here for you.

545
00:37:40,591 --> 00:37:41,968
The mailman?

546
00:37:44,971 --> 00:37:46,097
Brother Tongban.

547
00:37:46,639 --> 00:37:48,431
Brother Xiao's looking for you.

548
00:37:48,432 --> 00:37:50,101
Did you take the money?

549
00:37:50,601 --> 00:37:51,893
- What money?
- Who is he?

550
00:37:51,894 --> 00:37:53,311
- It's the--
- Step back.

551
00:37:53,312 --> 00:37:54,396
- What?
- Close your eyes.

552
00:37:54,397 --> 00:37:55,939
Shut the door. Back up.

553
00:37:55,940 --> 00:37:57,065
Okay, I'll close the door.

554
00:37:57,066 --> 00:37:57,983
Who is it?

555
00:37:57,984 --> 00:37:58,900
Step back.

556
00:37:58,901 --> 00:38:00,610
Don't come closer. Back up. Stay back.

557
00:38:00,611 --> 00:38:02,862
- Okay, I'll stay back. Calm down.
- What do you want?

558
00:38:02,863 --> 00:38:04,197
Where's the five million?

559
00:38:04,198 --> 00:38:05,240
Brother Xiao has it.

560
00:38:05,241 --> 00:38:07,826
Isn't there money in the safe?
Give me five million. Hurry.

561
00:38:07,827 --> 00:38:09,869
There may not be enough cash.

562
00:38:09,870 --> 00:38:12,163
Don't care. Get the money.
I'll kill your wife.

563
00:38:12,164 --> 00:38:13,581
- No!
- I'm not his wife.

564
00:38:13,582 --> 00:38:14,667
- Let go!
- Quiet.

565
00:38:16,043 --> 00:38:17,168
Is A-Li signaling us?

566
00:38:17,169 --> 00:38:18,211
He wants our help?

567
00:38:18,212 --> 00:38:20,380
No! Is Ruyi bleeding?

568
00:38:20,381 --> 00:38:22,257
I can't look. Is he your friend?

569
00:38:22,258 --> 00:38:23,800
Look at me!

570
00:38:23,801 --> 00:38:26,594
No, I'm shaking. I'm scared.

571
00:38:26,595 --> 00:38:28,847
I'm more scared! Get the money!

572
00:38:28,848 --> 00:38:30,724
Okay, calm down.

573
00:38:30,725 --> 00:38:31,975
Just go! We'll handle this.

574
00:38:31,976 --> 00:38:33,351
- We got this.
- Move!

575
00:38:33,352 --> 00:38:34,561
Okay.

576
00:38:34,562 --> 00:38:36,272
- Hurry, go!
- Okay.

577
00:38:42,695 --> 00:38:43,779
Turn around.

578
00:38:45,489 --> 00:38:47,366
Sit down.

579
00:38:48,826 --> 00:38:49,952
Do you have any rope?

580
00:38:52,038 --> 00:38:53,872
It's such a pain not having a phone.

581
00:38:53,873 --> 00:38:55,206
No phone is such a pain.

582
00:38:55,207 --> 00:38:56,499
- Is Brother Xiao here?
- Yeah.

583
00:38:56,500 --> 00:38:58,878
Spray me! Hurry...

584
00:39:01,756 --> 00:39:03,214
Brother Xiao...

585
00:39:03,215 --> 00:39:05,091
Hi, Sister Zhuzhu. Brother Xiao, I...

586
00:39:05,092 --> 00:39:07,177
- I'll take her out for some air.
- Okay, go.

587
00:39:07,178 --> 00:39:08,678
Be good.

588
00:39:08,679 --> 00:39:10,638
Well...

589
00:39:10,639 --> 00:39:11,849
Good girl.

590
00:39:12,975 --> 00:39:13,976
What is it?

591
00:39:15,227 --> 00:39:16,520
Where'd the baby come from?

592
00:39:21,192 --> 00:39:22,943
My wife doesn't know yet.

593
00:39:24,403 --> 00:39:27,739
This baby must be a gift from heaven.

594
00:39:27,740 --> 00:39:32,035
God knows how long
we've prayed for a child.

595
00:39:32,036 --> 00:39:36,873
Last week, someone left her
outside our door.

596
00:39:36,874 --> 00:39:39,334
You have to keep this secret, okay?

597
00:39:39,335 --> 00:39:40,586
Yes.

598
00:39:41,712 --> 00:39:46,174
- What's going on?
- The real problem is my wife won't sleep.

599
00:39:46,175 --> 00:39:49,886
She's afraid the baby may stop breathing,
so she stays up all night.

600
00:39:49,887 --> 00:39:52,931
A few days ago, the baby
had an allergic reaction and diarrhea.

601
00:39:52,932 --> 00:39:56,142
The doctor said
it was probably the formula,

602
00:39:56,143 --> 00:39:59,229
but my wife insists it's the best
because it's expensive.

603
00:39:59,230 --> 00:40:02,857
Now the baby's bottom is red and raw
from all the diarrhea and washing.

604
00:40:02,858 --> 00:40:04,777
I don't know what to do.

605
00:40:05,528 --> 00:40:07,028
I know she means well,

606
00:40:07,029 --> 00:40:09,489
but the baby's suffering.

607
00:40:09,490 --> 00:40:12,158
Brother Xiao,
want to try some <i>shuijie</i> milk?

608
00:40:12,159 --> 00:40:13,451
<i>Xuejie's</i> milk?

609
00:40:13,452 --> 00:40:14,869
<i>Shuijie</i> milk.

610
00:40:14,870 --> 00:40:16,496
Which of your <i>xuejies</i> has milk?

611
00:40:16,497 --> 00:40:17,832
Hydrolyzed formula.

612
00:40:18,749 --> 00:40:19,874
Hydrolyzed formula.

613
00:40:19,875 --> 00:40:21,918
- She usually drinks that.
- She?

614
00:40:21,919 --> 00:40:24,921
I mean, lots of babies drink it.

615
00:40:24,922 --> 00:40:27,550
Okay, I'll try it.

616
00:40:29,301 --> 00:40:30,594
What did you need me for?

617
00:40:32,346 --> 00:40:33,597
Tongban showed up.

618
00:40:34,390 --> 00:40:35,641
Where is he?

619
00:40:42,731 --> 00:40:43,941
I remember you.

620
00:40:44,650 --> 00:40:46,318
You're that hottie from the club.

621
00:40:47,153 --> 00:40:48,279
Remember me?

622
00:40:54,910 --> 00:40:57,872
You work with A-Li.
So is he a gangster too?

623
00:40:58,747 --> 00:41:00,248
You're way too innocent.

624
00:41:00,249 --> 00:41:03,085
You don't even know what he does,
yet you're with him?

625
00:41:03,794 --> 00:41:05,004
Why not choose me?

626
00:41:05,671 --> 00:41:08,340
I've got more of a future than A-Li...

627
00:41:10,384 --> 00:41:12,510
You think I'm scared of you?

628
00:41:12,511 --> 00:41:15,972
Brother Tongban fears nothing,
except ghosts.

629
00:41:15,973 --> 00:41:16,973
Perfect, then.

630
00:41:16,974 --> 00:41:17,974
Your hand?

631
00:41:17,975 --> 00:41:19,435
Creep!

632
00:41:20,144 --> 00:41:21,645
What's going on here?

633
00:41:23,189 --> 00:41:24,606
- Ghost!
- Get him!

634
00:41:24,607 --> 00:41:26,524
- Like a UFO?
- Calm down.

635
00:41:26,525 --> 00:41:27,859
Don't come any closer!

636
00:41:27,860 --> 00:41:29,110
That guy can't see us.

637
00:41:29,111 --> 00:41:31,488
Calm down. Your house is haunted!

638
00:41:31,489 --> 00:41:32,822
Please, I really...

639
00:41:32,823 --> 00:41:34,450
Stay back!

640
00:41:35,618 --> 00:41:39,079
Please, I'm scared of ghosts!

641
00:41:46,253 --> 00:41:48,839
Brother Xiao, you got it wrong.

642
00:41:50,382 --> 00:41:52,468
Tseng Yu-Li, you betrayed me too.

643
00:41:53,219 --> 00:41:54,260
Move aside!

644
00:41:54,261 --> 00:41:55,721
Brother Xiao, wait.

645
00:42:05,481 --> 00:42:06,857
<i>He's your boss.</i>

646
00:42:07,525 --> 00:42:10,110
Can't you ask him
to give Taozi back to us?

647
00:42:12,863 --> 00:42:14,489
No, that's not the point.

648
00:42:14,490 --> 00:42:16,950
Brother Xiao isn't the problem.

649
00:42:16,951 --> 00:42:18,994
It's his wife, Sister Zhuzhu.

650
00:42:20,996 --> 00:42:23,248
Should I talk to Sister Zhuzhu tomorrow?

651
00:42:23,249 --> 00:42:26,793
I'll apologize and ask for Taozi back.

652
00:42:26,794 --> 00:42:28,836
She's a mom too. She'll understand, right?

653
00:42:28,837 --> 00:42:30,130
Knowing her,

654
00:42:30,923 --> 00:42:33,175
she won't give Taozi back that easily.

655
00:42:36,512 --> 00:42:38,222
Don't worry.

656
00:42:39,139 --> 00:42:40,391
I'll think of something.

657
00:42:49,191 --> 00:42:50,525
Zhuzhu.

658
00:42:50,526 --> 00:42:51,944
Keep your voice down!

659
00:42:52,820 --> 00:42:54,071
Keep it down!

660
00:42:56,198 --> 00:43:00,159
It's over 30 degrees outside.
The baby's dressed too warmly.

661
00:43:00,160 --> 00:43:03,204
Enough talking. Go get us discharged.

662
00:43:03,205 --> 00:43:04,122
All right.

663
00:43:04,123 --> 00:43:05,207
Okay.

664
00:43:07,626 --> 00:43:08,793
Is the car here?

665
00:43:08,794 --> 00:43:10,045
Boss, it's here.

666
00:43:10,713 --> 00:43:11,921
Take everything to the car.

667
00:43:11,922 --> 00:43:13,173
- Hurry up.
- Yes.

668
00:43:15,676 --> 00:43:18,803
This folds. Don't throw it around.
Fold it before packing it.

669
00:43:18,804 --> 00:43:19,721
Yes, boss.

670
00:43:19,722 --> 00:43:21,472
She wants all these bottles.

671
00:43:21,473 --> 00:43:22,808
- Pack them well.
- Got it.

672
00:43:23,517 --> 00:43:25,102
Please give my daughter back.

673
00:43:27,563 --> 00:43:30,023
A DNA test can prove Taozi is my daughter.

674
00:43:30,024 --> 00:43:31,149
Then what?

675
00:43:31,150 --> 00:43:33,401
<i>Social services might take Taozi away.</i>

676
00:43:33,402 --> 00:43:34,569
<i>Even though I kept</i>

677
00:43:34,570 --> 00:43:36,696
<i>failing to have a baby,</i>

678
00:43:36,697 --> 00:43:39,283
<i>I never once thought about giving up.</i>

679
00:43:40,784 --> 00:43:41,994
Charge!

680
00:43:45,873 --> 00:43:46,706
Boss, it's here.

681
00:43:46,707 --> 00:43:47,624
Li Zhuzhu

682
00:43:47,625 --> 00:43:49,793
seems better suited to be her mother.

683
00:43:50,586 --> 00:43:53,005
Give me Taozi back.
